==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequired  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AuthRequired.als
    rationale: Clearing the auth boundary lets the model invent a successful operation with authenticated=False, which is exactly what AuthRequiredEverywhere is supposed to forbid.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_004_FlatPermissions
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_FlatPermissions: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyDeletions  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyDeletions.als
    rationale: Clearing the uniqueness constraints lets two TaskDeletion entries reference the same task, which is the canonical violation of an append-only log and permanent deletion.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_012_PermanentDeletion
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_PermanentDeletion: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeletionAuditCompleteness  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeletionAuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing audit completeness lets a successful delete op exist with no corresponding log entry, breaking the per-delete one-to-one audit invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_018_DeletionLogged
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_DeletionLogged: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AttributionCorrectness  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AttributionCorrectness.als
    rationale: Clearing the attribution fact lets a log entry record a deleter different from the actual op caller — exactly the misattribution case the assertion is designed to detect.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_IdentityFromContext  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_IdentityFromContext.als
    rationale: Clearing the identity-from-context fact lets a task's recorded creator diverge from its create-op's authenticated caller, modelling the payload-spoofing bug FR-002 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: FR_002_IdentityFromContext
      - FR_002_IdentityFromContext: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ClosedTaskEditRule  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_ClosedTaskEditRule.als
    rationale: Clearing the closed-task edit rule lets a successful edit on a Done task keep the status as Done, which is precisely the PATCH-on-closed bug FR-011 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule
      - FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule: FAIL (expected)

